; Directive file for makecab, used to build the cab file submitted to the
; Microsoft LSA file signing portal.
;
; Microsoft requires LSA submissions to be a single cabinet containing no
; folders and nothing but the binaries to be signed, so exactly one file goes
; in, stored as a bare "teleport.dll" with no path component. The two-token
; entry at the bottom is what guarantees that: the second token is the name the
; file is stored under, independent of where it was read from.
;
; The cabinet name is supplied by the Makefile via /D CabinetNameTemplate so
; that the DLL version lives in one place.

.OPTION EXPLICIT

.Set Cabinet=on
.Set Compress=on
.Set CompressionType=MSZIP

; No size limit, so the output is always a single cabinet rather than a split
; set. The portal accepts one file only.
.Set MaxDiskSize=0

; No signature reservation. osslsigncode appends the Authenticode signature and
; writes its own 20-byte header pointing at it; a ReservePerCabinetSize
; reservation sets cbCFHeader to that size instead, which osslsigncode rejects.

.Set DiskDirectory1=build

; Suppress the setup.rpt and setup.inf files makecab writes by default; they are
; build noise and must not end up in the cabinet.
.Set RptFileName=nul
.Set InfFileName=nul

installer\teleport.dll teleport.dll
